{"id":"37088e80-c904-43a6-b813-4240f274672f","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"The opcode parameter generally represents a byte opcode value within the 0 to 255 range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.413369376Z"}
{"id":"4966a2ef-e4fb-49ad-990e-8a68c127f43f","expr":"(opcode == 16) || (opcode == 17) || (opcode == 188)","rationale":"Based on ASM's IntInsn opcodes, opcode should be among valid int instruction opcodes.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.413369376Z"}
{"id":"f03b8903-ed83-4fe4-87b5-caac038b138b","expr":"operand >= 0","rationale":"Operands for int instructions like BIPUSH, SIPUSH, and NEWARRAY are non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.413369376Z"}
{"id":"0b1e7f35-cdf1-4c8a-9fb8-012776b3cd64","expr":"(opcode != 188) || (operand >= 4 && operand <= 11)","rationale":"When opcode is NEWARRAY, operand specifies array type code within specific range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.413369376Z"}
{"id":"ea017110-78fe-4607-91df-5f422e82edbe","expr":"(opcode == 16) || (opcode == 17) || (opcode == 188) || (opcode >= 188 && opcode <= 192)","rationale":"visitIntInsn is called with opcodes valid for the int instructions: BIPUSH(16), SIPUSH(17), NEWARRAY(188), etc.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.413617823Z"}
{"id":"fcbe606f-efa2-4725-ae3c-4443cecb568b","expr":"(opcode == 16 || opcode == 17) || (opcode == 188)","rationale":"Opcode for this method should be one of the opcodes that expect a single int operand.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.413369376Z"}
{"id":"ee2ab1e2-ee21-4a5f-ba8b-cad68e8950de","expr":"(opcode == 16 && operand >= -128 && operand <= 127) || (opcode == 17 && operand >= -32768 && operand <= 32767) || (opcode == 188 && operand >= 4 && operand <= 11)","rationale":"For BIPUSH(16), operand fits in a byte; for SIPUSH(17), operand fits in a short; for NEWARRAY(188), operand defines primitive array type within specific range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.413617823Z"}
{"id":"ecc2f9d5-858e-485c-9488-3178ab190607","expr":"opcode != 0","rationale":"opcode zero typically is not a valid opcode for visitIntInsn.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.413617823Z"}
{"id":"d88c7323-a9de-4173-b4a5-02c7c58ea2ad","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"The opcode is an unsigned byte representing the bytecode instruction.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.418499544Z"}
{"id":"ef3af68e-051f-4bfa-940a-b55c8cb92422","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Local variable indexes in JVM bytecode are non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.418499544Z"}
{"id":"1d0d503d-bd40-403f-9227-f0eb8c43b3c6","expr":"opcode != 0","rationale":"It is likely that opcode should represent a valid instruction, not zero.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.418499544Z"}
{"id":"b0f9c52b-6635-46e2-aaea-0aecae42f6c0","expr":"varIndex < 256","rationale":"Local variable indexes are typically in byte range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.418499544Z"}
{"id":"34581959-e4fd-4fd7-987e-13433c3f3967","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"The opcode represents a JVM instruction opcode which validly ranges between 0 and 255.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.418893255Z"}
{"id":"41d79f86-58f5-4c0c-bf68-1e1bfe564ca4","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"The varIndex represents a local variable slot index which cannot be negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.418893255Z"}
{"id":"665c9345-3594-4499-9f6d-b192a59728ab","expr":"varIndex <= 65535","rationale":"In JVM spec, local variable indices are stored as unsigned 16-bit values so varIndex should be in this range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.418893255Z"}
{"id":"c3f586aa-3645-4b55-8198-ef2e8db2e09c","expr":"!(opcode < 0)","rationale":"opcode values are never negative because they represent unsigned byte instruction codes.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.418893255Z"}
{"id":"668e2793-b8af-4df3-bf31-85f5584f9125","expr":"type != null && type.length() > 0","rationale":"type is expected to be a valid internal class name or descriptor string.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.420876930Z"}
