{"id":"50538f1d-62bb-4040-b57f-1914f9ee1335","expr":"opcode != 0","rationale":"Opcode zero typically does not represent any valid jump instruction opcode.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.430886354Z"}
{"id":"dac82f61-1d3f-488a-8639-6192fe3b7124","expr":"label.getOffset() >= 0","rationale":"A Label's offset field marks position in bytecode and should be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.430886354Z"}
{"id":"20ad1ebd-4860-4ace-a918-24cf877339a3","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcodes in ASM are generally non-negative integers representing a valid instruction.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.431443513Z"}
{"id":"832d3f7f-77f4-43cb-9499-ba1c9eb786e2","expr":"label != null","rationale":"A jump instruction must have a valid target label, so label is non-null when this method returns.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.431443513Z"}
{"id":"f5c8eb35-b697-4f8b-acde-a77bec5b5e00","expr":"opcode != 167 || label != null","rationale":"If opcode equals GOTO (167), label must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.431443513Z"}
{"id":"96acc5bf-20d6-440e-9739-a515d65896b5","expr":"opcode >= 153 && opcode <= 166 || opcode == 198 || opcode == 199","rationale":"Opcode is within the range or set of known jump instruction codes.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.431443513Z"}
{"id":"3ee51225-fdd9-4c47-9b10-c13ba264b92c","expr":"!(opcode < 153 || (opcode > 166 && opcode != 198 && opcode != 199))","rationale":"Ensures opcode is a recognized jump instruction code.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.431443513Z"}
{"id":"7d172a28-c889-45e1-9511-f147d0c5af70","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The method uses the label parameter directly, so it must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.433187847Z"}
{"id":"b4c69e33-2af7-4854-bfca-9499cb84067c","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The method processes a label that it expects to be non-null to function properly.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.433786254Z"}
{"id":"c4536ec1-39fb-4269-a33b-02cc945b7471","expr":"label.info == null || label.position >= 0","rationale":"If label.info is null, the label has probably not yet been assigned a position; else, the position should be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.433786254Z"}
{"id":"19112d1f-846a-4ef3-8f7b-92777da20ad8","expr":"label.sourcePosition >= 0 || label.info == null","rationale":"Labels with info generally have a valid source position.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.433786254Z"}
{"id":"a478f4b7-db28-4173-9237-ead7f4122c4c","expr":"label.frame == null || label.frame.owner == label","rationale":"If the label manages frames, those frames should correctly reference their parent label.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.433786254Z"}
{"id":"e6d21b9e-5664-4856-b1f2-07fc89883bf8","expr":"label.successors == null || label.successors.length >= 0","rationale":"If the label has successors, the array length must be non-negative since length is never negative in Java arrays.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.433786254Z"}
{"id":"9c6055bd-f501-4d64-99a3-8f45c5ecf6ee","expr":"value != null || value == null","rationale":"Value can be any object or null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.435779146Z"}
{"id":"f748a457-85be-4c78-92ba-a2656f66faff","expr":"value != null","rationale":"In general usage, value passed to visitLdcInsn is expected to be non-null as null constants are not handled as operands.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.436805638Z"}
{"id":"c7e07d9e-9869-4c1f-ad26-e15304cad05e","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Local variables in bytecode are indexed from zero upwards, so varIndex should be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.438121425Z"}
{"id":"bec3bfd9-882c-48e2-97c2-3a79ef5c6a8e","expr":"increment != 0","rationale":"IINC with a zero increment means no change, so increment is expected to be non-zero.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.438121425Z"}
{"id":"ed2ae66a-ba5e-418e-826d-b89816d9058a","expr":"increment >= Byte.MIN_VALUE && increment <= Byte.MAX_VALUE","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, the increment is a signed byte between -128 and 127.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.438121425Z"}
{"id":"e029f746-0506-4376-bd23-a18b20bb3150","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, variable indexes used in instructions like IINC are non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.438741453Z"}
{"id":"d9a4ba6a-6bfd-4835-89fa-10f49f9a539f","expr":"increment != 0","rationale":"The IINC instruction increments a local variable by a non-zero amount to have effect.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.438741453Z"}
{"id":"a5a6fc29-db3e-4e25-854b-5550f2844a6b","expr":"Math.abs(increment) <= 127","rationale":"The JVM specification limits the increment operand in IINC instruction to a signed 8-bit value.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.438741453Z"}
{"id":"8b1f62d5-836c-4af5-829d-abafae477151","expr":"varIndex <= 65535","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, the variable index is generally limited to 16-bit unsigned values.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.438741453Z"}
{"id":"28ae6613-9094-4c35-b739-30f9ab311699","expr":"max >= min","rationale":"The max value should be greater or equal to the min value for a valid table switch range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.439569271Z"}
{"id":"2c96cea9-d630-4271-a926-3c0ca0a188a5","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels array must be non-null as it contains the jump targets.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.439569271Z"}
{"id":"740afec9-c5bd-4128-974b-c9cfda01eeec","expr":"labels.length >= (max - min + 1)","rationale":"The number of labels should at least cover the range from min to max inclusive.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.439569271Z"}
{"id":"513846df-8c5a-4f59-b1d3-8c30d833c597","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label must be non-null as the default jump target.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.439569271Z"}
{"id":"4f12e61c-db1c-4ccd-87de-495b84984e12","expr":"max >= min","rationale":"The table switch bounds must maintain max greater or equal to min to represent a valid range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.440170523Z"}
{"id":"bfc864d7-66c8-430a-b36a-755efc165021","expr":"labels.length == max - min + 1","rationale":"The labels array length should be exactly max - min + 1 for the table switch mapping.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.440170523Z"}
{"id":"95f5d2d3-6d5e-46e8-aa0e-8afdc0b3b0d2","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label for the table switch must not be null as it is the fallback branch.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.440170523Z"}
{"id":"82e169fa-bf2e-4eb6-af9d-cafd5a77e3a0","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels array must be non-null because it provides the jump targets for the switch.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.440170523Z"}
{"id":"4b8ef89a-2335-4c36-be9b-535047501824","expr":"min <= max + 1","rationale":"To allow for valid or empty ranges, min is allowed to be at most max + 1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.440170523Z"}
{"id":"e20d185b-ef6c-4ab6-b68c-7f4d6a10c537","expr":"keys != null","rationale":"The keys array is essential for the lookup switch to have values to match keys against.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.441467956Z"}
{"id":"9b6595f6-48d7-4364-802b-e5bdc3e67b0c","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"Labels provide jump targets for the matching keys.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.441467956Z"}
{"id":"771bbc0d-b9a5-49c0-8c98-18f6fe97e0c7","expr":"labels.length == keys.length","rationale":"The keys and labels arrays are matched pairwise by index.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.441467956Z"}
{"id":"95c2fc13-4166-4abd-9a7e-337ffcd453f1","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label is the fall-through target.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.441467956Z"}
{"id":"aeabbeba-42e2-438e-9eb7-00de5e66e61f","expr":"keys.length >= 0","rationale":"Safety invariant about array length.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.441467956Z"}
{"id":"39d72ebb-af33-4833-8479-c608bd2de7fb","expr":"keys == null || labels != null","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, the number of keys and labels correspond to switch cases, so labels should not be null if keys exist.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.442578857Z"}
{"id":"3e501012-0c02-4da2-b358-2e533885716f","expr":"keys == null || labels.length == keys.length","rationale":"Each key corresponds to one label in the lookup switch, so their lengths must be equal.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.442578857Z"}
{"id":"2e68c730-8476-412a-93b7-037722e32fec","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"A lookup switch requires a default label to jump to when keys don't match.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.442578857Z"}
{"id":"a7183a78-4eaf-43f9-aafc-921597e46f25","expr":"keys == null || keys.length > 0","rationale":"It is not meaningful to have an empty keys array for the lookup switch; if present, keys array has positive length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.442578857Z"}
{"id":"ea94f6d6-c9ef-4cd9-87ab-9b75b5cfd9c7","expr":"labels == null || labels.length > 0","rationale":"Labels array corresponds to switch cases and should have positive length if not null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.442578857Z"}
{"id":"1d8e594c-0c29-422d-a1ea-c64afcb8021a","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The method is expected to handle a non-null descriptor string specifying the array type.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.445158754Z"}
{"id":"3ba33e0d-eaa0-47dc-93b4-fc54699c4c12","expr":"numDimensions > 0","rationale":"numDimensions represents the array dimensions and must be at least 1 to define a valid multi-dimensional array.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.445158754Z"}
{"id":"a0fe3fa7-dc99-402b-9699-ae04e3fb8ad0","expr":"numDimensions <= descriptor.length()","rationale":"The descriptor must encode the array type such that the number of dimensions does not exceed the descriptor length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.445158754Z"}
{"id":"60ae9938-4609-455e-b978-56b6a43208f0","expr":"descriptor.startsWith(\"[\")","rationale":"The descriptor for a multi-dimensional array starts with one or more '[' characters, one per dimension.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.445158754Z"}
{"id":"cb15cf8a-12a8-46b0-a6c6-7059ebc2b79a","expr":"descriptor.length() >= numDimensions + 1","rationale":"The descriptor has a prefix for every dimension plus a character for the base type; thus length should be at least numDimensions + 1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.445158754Z"}
{"id":"8866ead6-2492-4340-9ad1-062a2f6c36b5","expr":"!visible || result != null","rationale":"If the annotation is visible (visible is true), then the method is expected to return a non-null AnnotationVisitor.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsnAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.447316206Z"}
{"id":"2aadb205-40c9-4373-9572-c8ce0fbd9922","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The descriptor parameter is typically a non-null string describing the annotation.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsnAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.447424009Z"}
{"id":"04888977-1087-434b-b113-802aaae44c29","expr":"typePath == null || typePath.getLength() >= 0","rationale":"If typePath is present, its length is non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsnAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.447424009Z"}
{"id":"f9b437fc-986a-4f10-9ca4-df1bf78d2599","expr":"visible == true || visible == false","rationale":"visible is a boolean parameter, so it can only be true or false.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsnAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.447424009Z"}
{"id":"d49c8529-eb89-4792-becc-f5e780e8d608","expr":"typeRef >= 0","rationale":"typeRef typically encodes a reference and is non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsnAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.447424009Z"}
{"id":"77be718f-6bfa-4481-b770-44ee713f40ef","expr":"start != null","rationale":"The start label marks the beginning of the try block and must exist.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.448190993Z"}
{"id":"6085bbe8-9f47-4c84-a866-62aec6d775a5","expr":"end != null","rationale":"The end label marks the end of the try block and must exist.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.448190993Z"}
{"id":"65aab2ae-d240-47d6-a800-70c863b5c4f2","expr":"handler != null","rationale":"The exception handler label must be present to catch exceptions.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.448190993Z"}
{"id":"6348256d-2b11-42a5-b383-af6d6abaa29f","expr":"start.getOffset() <= end.getOffset()","rationale":"The start label must not be positioned after the end of the try block.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.448190993Z"}
{"id":"b5b765fc-d84a-4f8f-8d04-417368936a76","expr":"(type == null) || (!type.isEmpty())","rationale":"If type is non-null, it typically identifies the exception class and should not be empty.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.448190993Z"}
{"id":"dacca461-8ff8-487a-ace8-cc5c3a81b844","expr":"start != null","rationale":"start label for try block should be non-null since it's mandatory to define the start of try range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.448823574Z"}
{"id":"c2432884-94ae-48fd-ac3d-fc9273b2b10d","expr":"end != null","rationale":"end label for try block should be non-null as the range needs an end.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.448823574Z"}
{"id":"7c95c74a-2826-413e-a9a4-c78ad85085d9","expr":"handler != null","rationale":"handler label must be non-null since it defines the start of the catch block.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.448823574Z"}
{"id":"d0428658-b7d0-4d4f-a60c-b8b1f93cb01b","expr":"!start.equals(end)","rationale":"The try block's start and end labels should differ, defining a non-empty instruction range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.448823574Z"}
{"id":"04d61063-94a1-4afb-9dc4-a30c56825f9c","expr":"type == null || type.length() > 0","rationale":"The type is either null (catching all exceptions) or a non-empty fully qualified class name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.448823574Z"}
{"id":"03930e43-d1e4-4e48-a40e-68d8f6979813","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The descriptor should be a valid descriptor string indicating the annotation type.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.450151835Z"}
{"id":"b3f77b15-d998-434a-bd8d-fd814c4fcdd5","expr":"typePath == null || typePath.isEmpty() == false","rationale":"If typePath is provided, it typically represents a non-empty path; otherwise, it can be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.450151835Z"}
{"id":"2e1fe850-05b5-4da4-8345-dc0b22d33c5f","expr":"typeRef >= 0","rationale":"Type references in ASM are usually non-negative integers representing bytecode elements.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.450151835Z"}
{"id":"de80c9cd-17df-4cfa-90f9-2c1b9f8f1da8","expr":"visible == true || visible == false","rationale":"The visible parameter indicates the visibility of the annotation and must be boolean; this expression is tautological but acceptable for completeness.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.450151835Z"}
{"id":"535adf80-0d6e-4bbc-ab71-77bc3e36989a","expr":"typeRef <= 0xFFFFFFF","rationale":"Ensures that typeRef fits within the expected bit pattern used for type references in ASM.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:38:05.450151835Z"}
